# core/data/talk/grammar/en/quests.tlk - TQ-QUESTS: a resident raises a request and answers what you say to it (owner: TK;
# docs/TALK.md 6q; owner decision 2026-11-15 "TALK QUESTS"). The entry is `quest` (talk_gen_quest); the drama manager
# (talk_dm.c DK_QUEST) picks the phase and the kind, the rules below are guarded by them:
#   qphase=ask          the request, said by the resident after an answer (a question: the talk goes to the player)
#   qphase=accept       the player said yes
#   qphase=decline      the player said no (no guilt: a request is a favour, never a duty)
#   qphase=haggle_yes   "what's in it for me?" and the resident gives in
#   qphase=haggle_no    ... and does not (the request stands)
#   qphase=more         "tell me more" (qkind says what the request is)
#   qphase=done         the player hands it in (qkind says what it was)
#   qphase=late         a reminder when you meet again with it still open
#   qphase=expired      it ran out of days: "never mind"
#   qkind=fetch toy message company cheer peace secret
# Slots: {item} the item a fetch or toy is about, {target} the one a message, a cheer-up or a making-up is about.
# Kid-safe everywhere (a child says these too): a snack, a toy, a hello, company, a friend who is down. peace and secret
# are raised only for adults in adult rooms (talk_quest.c); their lines are clean as well. No register word, no romance,
# no place to go, no danger, no guilt for saying no.

# ---- ask --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule quest.ask.fetch guard: qphase=ask&qkind=fetch act: ask_about
  "Could you bring me {item:indef}? I would owe you one."
  "I'm dreaming of {item:indef}. Any chance you could fetch me one?"
  "Quick favour: find me {item:indef}? My legs have filed a complaint."
  "Would you grab me {item:indef} sometime? I'd remember it. Fondly."
@rule quest.ask.toy guard: qphase=ask&qkind=toy act: ask_about
  "I lost my toy. Could you find me {item:indef}? Please?"
  "Can you help me? I need {item:indef} to play with. Do you have one?"
  "Do you have {item:indef}? I would trade you a really good secret handshake."
  "My toy went on holiday without me. Could you bring me {item:indef}?"
@rule quest.ask.message guard: qphase=ask&qkind=message act: ask_about
  "Could you say hi to {target} for me? I'm too shy to wave."
  "Will you tell {target} I said hello? I keep forgetting to."
  "Do me a favour? Find {target} and say I was asking after them."
  "Pass a hello to {target} for me? You're so much better at hellos."
@rule quest.ask.company guard: qphase=ask&qkind=company act: ask_about
  "Would you come back and chat a while? A few minutes. No agenda."
  "Could you keep me company properly sometime? I miss a good long chat."
  "Say, would you stay and talk with me for a bit? Not just a wave."
  "I'd love some company. Would you sit with me and talk a while?"
@rule quest.ask.cheer guard: qphase=ask&qkind=cheer act: ask_about
  "{target:cap} seems a bit down. Could you cheer {target} up for me?"
  "I'm worried about {target}. Would you go and cheer them up?"
  "{target:cap} could use a friendly face. Would you find {target} and chat?"
  "Could you lift {target}'s spirits? Nothing big. A kind word works."
@rule quest.ask.peace guard: qphase=ask&qkind=peace act: ask_about
  "{target:cap} and I aren't speaking. Could you help us make up?"
  "Could you smooth things over with {target} for me? It got silly."
  "I hate this feud with {target}. Would you talk us back together?"
  "Would you play peacemaker between {target} and me? I'll owe you."
@rule quest.ask.secret guard: qphase=ask&qkind=secret act: ask_about
  "Can you keep a secret? Don't ask what. Just hold it for me a day."
  "I need someone trustworthy. Could you keep something quiet for a day?"
  "Would you keep a little secret for me? Just till tomorrow. Please?"
  "You seem like a vault. Could you keep my secret for a day?"

# ---- accept -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule quest.accept guard: qphase=accept act: tell
  "Thank you! I'll be right here. Not going anywhere, mostly."
  "You're a star. Take your time, but not too much."
  "Deal! You've made my whole day. Possibly my week."
  "Oh, bless you. I won't forget this."
  "Wonderful. I'll tell the fog how helpful you are."
  "You're the best. Come find me when it's done."

# ---- decline ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule quest.decline guard: qphase=decline act: tell
  "No worries. I'll sort it out myself."
  "Fair enough. Maybe another day."
  "That's okay. Thanks for hearing me out."
  "All right. I'll ask the fog. It never says no."
  "No problem. It was only a thought."
  "Understood. Let's just chat, then."

# ---- haggle: what is in it for me ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule quest.haggle_yes guard: qphase=haggle_yes act: ask_about
  "Ha, fair. I'll make it worth your while. So, deal?"
  "You drive a hard bargain. Fine, there's a bonus. Deal?"
  "Okay, okay, I'll add a little extra. Do we have a deal?"
  "Smart. All right, you'll get more than you'd expect. Deal?"
@rule quest.haggle_no guard: qphase=haggle_no act: ask_about
  "Oh, you want a deal? Take it or leave it. So, are you in?"
  "My thanks is the deal. A very good thanks. Are you in?"
  "That's all I've got, I'm afraid. Still in?"
  "No more bargaining, I'm out of bargain. Will you help?"

# ---- more: tell me more ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule quest.more.fetch guard: qphase=more&qkind=fetch act: tell
  "It's only {item:indef}. Nothing fancy. Just bring it when you have one."
  "Any {item} works. Fresh, stale, I'm not fussy. Okay, slightly fussy."
  "Look in the shop or your bag. If you have {item:indef}, just say."
@rule quest.more.toy guard: qphase=more&qkind=toy act: tell
  "It's {item:indef}. I only need one. I'll take very good care of it."
  "Mine's gone missing. A new one is fine, if you have {item:indef}."
  "I like playing with it before bed. Just bring {item:indef}, okay?"
@rule quest.more.message guard: qphase=more&qkind=message act: tell
  "Just say I was asking after them. That's all. You can't get it wrong."
  "Find {target} and say hello from me. Then come back. Easy!"
  "{target:cap} is easy to talk to, once you start. A hello is plenty."
@rule quest.more.company guard: qphase=more&qkind=company act: tell
  "Come back and talk a few minutes. About anything. The fog is fine."
  "I'm not asking for much. Just a good, long chat. A few minutes."
  "Sit, talk, laugh a bit. That's the whole favour."
@rule quest.more.cheer guard: qphase=more&qkind=cheer act: tell
  "{target:cap} had a rough day. A kind chat will do wonders."
  "No big plan. Just find {target} and be nice. You're good at nice."
  "Make {target} smile. Even a small one counts. I'm not picky."
@rule quest.more.peace guard: qphase=more&qkind=peace act: tell
  "It was a silly argument, honestly. A friendly word from you should do it."
  "We both said things. Mostly me. Help us talk it through?"
  "Nobody's winning this one. Just get {target} and me talking again."
@rule quest.more.secret guard: qphase=more&qkind=secret act: tell
  "I can't say what it is. Just don't tell anyone. A whole day."
  "It's only a little secret. But it matters to me. Just don't tell."
  "You don't have to do anything. Just don't blab. Then say hello tomorrow."

# ---- done: handing it in --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule quest.done.fetch guard: qphase=done&qkind=fetch act: tell
  "Is that {item:indef}? You legend. Thank you so much!"
  "You brought {item:indef}! I could hug you. Is that allowed?"
@rule quest.done.toy guard: qphase=done&qkind=toy act: tell
  "You found one! Thank you, thank you, thank you!"
  "Yay! {item:indef}! You're the best friend ever!"
@rule quest.done.message guard: qphase=done&qkind=message act: tell
  "You told {target}? Perfect. I can finally breathe again."
  "Thank you for saying hi to {target}. That was brave of you. And me."
@rule quest.done.company guard: qphase=done&qkind=company act: tell
  "Thanks for staying and talking. I needed that."
  "That was a lovely chat. I feel lighter already."
@rule quest.done.cheer guard: qphase=done&qkind=cheer act: tell
  "I heard you cheered {target} up. You're good at this."
  "Thank you for being kind to {target}. It really mattered."
@rule quest.done.peace guard: qphase=done&qkind=peace act: tell
  "{target:cap} and I are talking again. Because of you. Wow."
  "You got {target} and me to make up. I owe you big."
@rule quest.done.secret guard: qphase=done&qkind=secret act: tell
  "A whole day and not a peep. I trust you now."
  "You kept it. Honestly, I'm impressed. Thank you."

# ---- late: a reminder when you meet again ------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule quest.late guard: qphase=late act: ask_about
  "Any luck with that favour? No pressure. Some pressure."
  "Remember that little favour? No rush. Little rush."
  "I've been thinking about my favour. Have you had a minute?"
  "How's my favour coming along? I'm not counting. Much."

# ---- expired: it ran out of days -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule quest.expired guard: qphase=expired act: tell
  "Never mind about that favour. I managed. Really."
  "Oh, the favour? Forget it. It's totally fine."
  "I sorted my little favour out. No hard feelings. Mostly."
  "Don't worry about that favour any more. Life goes on."
